# Untracked working material, all of it reproducible or re-clonable:
#   misc/tpcdi/            upstream TPC-DI clone (format-contract reference)
#   misc/sample_run/       generated output, reproducible from a seed
#   misc/tpcdi_out/        extracted upstream material
#   misc/abandoned-tpcds/  the dropped TPC-DS direction
misc/

# Python environments. Machine-specific, regenerated from pyproject.toml.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.ruff_cache/

# Large binaries, wherever they land. A database dump has no place in history.
*.db
*.duckdb
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Transient scratch. The durable parts of .scratch/coursework/ are the map,
# its tickets, and the research notes, and those are tracked explicitly.
.scratch/**/*.tmp
.scratch/**/tmp/

# Local overrides and secrets. None committed; this is here so a stray .env
# cannot land by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Exception: infra/.env is the platform's configuration, not a secret file.
# Every value in it is a local development default, there is no production
# credential anywhere in this repository, and Docker Compose reads it at parse
# time, so without it a fresh clone has no port map and no service config. Copy
# it and edit locally if you need to; do not put a real credential in it.
!infra/.env

# Course-side material and the session-local collaboration file. These are
# reference documents and working notes, not the project itself; they stay on
# disk where nothing outside this machine can copy them.
AGENTS.md
docs/course/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/